{
  "schema": "ccc.memory-artifact-inventory.v1",
  "note": "#873 step-1 inventory. Machine-readable policy registration for every private/body-bearing artifact class the harness writes. Paths are RESOLVER CHAINS (first existing candidate wins), never globs — an apply slice must go through these same chains, never raw $HOME expansion. Fields: role (source|derived|outbox|audit|index|operational), owner, requests (lifecycle request -> action; 'external-handoff' means a node-local run must not touch it). related_dirs (optional, dir-kind entries): sibling directories owned by the same class — classified alongside the resolved dir, never flagged unknown. extra_paths (optional, file-kind entries): additional literal candidates owned by the SAME class (multi-file classes like the managed cron logs) — classified, estimated and targeted per path. resolve candidates may also carry kind=pattern: an ANCHORED regex over sibling file names under the candidate's base (join form: env is the base; absolute form: dirname is the base) — lets one class own dated artifacts (bench-YYYYMMDD.md) without inventing files; name matching only, never glob expansion.",
